---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import H1 from "../components/text/H1.astro";
import H2 from "../components/text/H2.astro";
import H3 from "../components/text/H3.astro";
import Text from "../components/text/Text.astro";


const schemaMarkup = {

}

const headContent ={
  metaTitle: "About WebCharged | Yuma Web Agency for Small Businesses",
  metaDescription: "We believe in honesty and fairness. We want to partner with small businesses to help them grow. Your success is our success.",
  schemaMarkup,
}

---

<MainLayout headContent={headContent}>
  <section class="flex justify-center bg-blue-gradient px-32 md:px-53 lg:px-59 py-85 md:py-223 lg:py-249">
    <div class="grow-1 flex flex-col gap-20 lg:gap-22 max-w-1281">
      <H1>Recent Work</H1>
      <Text class="text-parchment max-w-450 md:max-w-550 lg:max-w-600">
        Check out the custom websites we have built recently. 
        For each project, we dedicated many hours to get the exact website the client wanted.
      </Text> 
    </div>
  </section> 
  <section id="project1-section1" class="flex justify-center px-32 md:px-53 lg:px-59 py-59 md:py-95 bg-charcoal">
    <div class="grow-1 flex flex-col items-center gap-59 max-w-559 md:max-w-1032 xl:max-w-1281">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-14 items-center">
        <H2 color="electric">RSKI Riders</H2>
        <p class="font-semibold text-parchment">Website Redesign — 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="w-full flex flex-col md:flex-row md:flex-wrap lg:flex-nowrap justify-center items-center md:items-start gap-x-36 gap-y-59">

        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-14 w-full md:w-400 lg:w-500 grow lg:grow-0 shrink-0 md:max-w-500">
          <img
            src="/images/rski-website-on-laptop.jpg" 
            alt="Image of the RSKI Riders website on a laptop screen" 
            width="500" 
            height="288" 
            loading="lazy"
            class="w-full"
          >

          <div class="flex flex-row gap-5 items-center">
            <a href="https://rskiriders.com" target="_blank" class="text-16/[175%] font-semibold text-electric hover:underline focus:underline focus-visible:underline">Visit the live website</a>

            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <mask id="mask0_4470_14251" style="mask-type:alpha" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="0" y="0" width="14" height="14">
              <rect width="14" height="14" fill="#D9D9D9"/>
              </mask>
              <g mask="url(#mask0_4470_14251)">
              <path d="M3.01458 12.5303C2.58389 12.5303 2.21858 12.3803 1.91865 12.0804C1.61872 11.7805 1.46875 11.4152 1.46875 10.9845V3.01556C1.46875 2.58487 1.61872 2.21955 1.91865 1.91962C2.21858 1.61969 2.58389 1.46973 3.01458 1.46973H6.99904V3.01556H3.01458V10.9845H10.9835V7.00002H12.5293V10.9845C12.5293 11.4152 12.3794 11.7805 12.0794 12.0804C11.7795 12.3803 11.4142 12.5303 10.9835 12.5303H3.01458ZM5.91287 9.15835L4.84071 8.08618L9.91119 3.01556H8.16571V1.46973H12.5293V5.83335H10.9835V4.08787L5.91287 9.15835Z" fill="#FF9D0A"/>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-22 md:w-364 grow shrink-0 max-w-644 lg:max-w-none">
          <H3 color="parchment">About RSKI Riders</H3>

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
            <p class="text-parchment text-16 xl:text-19">
              RSKI Riders makes custom aftermarket parts for jet skis and motorcycles. 
              RSKI was started by two engineers with a passion for jet ski riding.
            </p>
            <p class="text-parchment text-16 xl:text-19">
              They found problems with the parts on their jet skis. 
              And what was their solution? Make their own parts!
            </p>
            <p class="text-parchment text-16 xl:text-19">
              One of their most popular products is their custom-engineered jet ski throttle. 
              Hours and hours of time was invested to make this throttle perfect for jet ski riding.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="project1-section2" class="flex justify-center px-32 md:px-53 lg:px-59 py-59 md:py-95">
    <div class="grow-1 flex flex-col-reverse md:flex-row md:flex-wrap-reverse justify-center items-center gap-95 max-w-559 md:max-w-1281">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-36 w-full md:w-349 md:grow md:shrink-0 md:max-w-644 lg:max-w-none">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
          <H3>The Challenge</H3>
          <p class="text-16">
            RSKI Riders had some problems with their old website. 
            They built it themselves using Wix, and it was mostly accomplishing everything they wanted — 
            but it wasn’t quite perfect.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">1.</span>
              <p>
                <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">The homepage.</span> One of the RSKI guys built the homepage the best he could. He had an idea of what he wanted, 
                but he wasn’t able to replicate that vision. As a result, the homepage was not being used for its best potential.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">2.</span>
              <p>
                <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">Reviews.</span> Their current website wasn’t collecting or displaying any reviews at all. 
                Wix did give them this functionality, but they weren’t happy with it so they removed the reviews-collecting feature.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">3.</span>
              <p>
                <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">Product Pages.</span> They needed to add more detail to their product pages (especially for the jet ski throttle). 
                They wanted to highlight different features of each product, showing images with descriptive text. 
                But Wix didn’t let them do this. So they created a complicated work-around to get what they wanted. 
                But it was a pain to create product pages like that.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
          <H3>The Solution</H3>
          <p class="text-16">
            To solve their problems, we built RSKI Riders a custom website using Shopify.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">1.</span>
              <p>
                First, we created a detailed website prototype 
                and planned out exactly what the homepage, category, and product pages would look like.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">2.</span>
              <p>
                Then we took a starter Shopify theme, and modified it with custom, hand-written Liquid code. 
                This allowed us to match the website prototype we created perfectly.  
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">3.</span>
              <p>
                We modified the default product page template to fit their vision. 
                So now the RSKI guys can <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">easily</span> add extended descriptions for the features of their products.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">4.</span>
              <p>
                We also installed a Shopify app for collecting and displaying reviews. 
                It works great and fits well with the website design.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
          <H3>The Results</H3>
          <p class="text-16">
            RSKI Riders now has a professional website <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">that they can be proud of</span>. 
            Now people get a great first impression of RSKI when they visit the website. 
            The design communicates that RSKI is a serious business that sells valuable products. 
            Their website is helping to equip their business for growth.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-59 w-full max-w-300 shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/rski-website-on-mobile.png" 
          alt="Image of the RSKI Riders website on a mobile phone screen" 
          width="300" 
          height="602" 
          loading="lazy"
          class="w-full"
        >

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
          <p class="italic text-16 md:text-21">
            “This is a great spot for a quote or a review if applicable. 
            Larger words. Italics. Says something fantastic about the website or about working with WebCharged.”
          </p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-16 md:text-21">— John Smith</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="project2-section1" class="flex justify-center px-32 md:px-53 lg:px-59 py-59 md:py-95 bg-charcoal">
    <div class="grow-1 flex flex-col items-center gap-59 max-w-559 md:max-w-1032 xl:max-w-1281">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-14 items-center">
        <H2 color="electric">Freedom Christian Preschool</H2>
        <p class="font-semibold text-parchment">New Website — 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="w-full flex flex-col md:flex-row md:flex-wrap lg:flex-nowrap justify-center items-center md:items-start gap-x-36 gap-y-59">

        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-14 w-full md:w-400 lg:w-500 grow lg:grow-0 shrink-0 md:max-w-500">
          <img
            src="/images/rski-website-on-laptop.jpg" 
            alt="Image of the RSKI Riders website on a laptop screen" 
            width="500" 
            height="288" 
            loading="lazy"
            class="w-full"
          >

          <div class="flex flex-row gap-5 items-center">
            <a href="https://fcpyuma.org" target="_blank" class="text-16/[175%] font-semibold text-electric hover:underline focus:underline focus-visible:underline">Visit the live website</a>

            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <mask id="mask0_4470_14251" style="mask-type:alpha" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="0" y="0" width="14" height="14">
              <rect width="14" height="14" fill="#D9D9D9"/>
              </mask>
              <g mask="url(#mask0_4470_14251)">
              <path d="M3.01458 12.5303C2.58389 12.5303 2.21858 12.3803 1.91865 12.0804C1.61872 11.7805 1.46875 11.4152 1.46875 10.9845V3.01556C1.46875 2.58487 1.61872 2.21955 1.91865 1.91962C2.21858 1.61969 2.58389 1.46973 3.01458 1.46973H6.99904V3.01556H3.01458V10.9845H10.9835V7.00002H12.5293V10.9845C12.5293 11.4152 12.3794 11.7805 12.0794 12.0804C11.7795 12.3803 11.4142 12.5303 10.9835 12.5303H3.01458ZM5.91287 9.15835L4.84071 8.08618L9.91119 3.01556H8.16571V1.46973H12.5293V5.83335H10.9835V4.08787L5.91287 9.15835Z" fill="#FF9D0A"/>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-22 md:w-364 grow shrink-0 max-w-644 lg:max-w-none">
          <H3 color="parchment">About</H3>

          <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
            <p class="text-parchment text-16 xl:text-19">
              Freedom Christian Preschool is a new Christian preschool in Yuma, AZ and is a ministry of Freedom Baptist Church.
            </p>
            <p class="text-parchment text-16 xl:text-19">
              Freedom Christian Preschool is committed to providing excellent care for the children in their preschool. 
              Their goal is that each child develops a love for learning to prepare them for kindergarten.
            </p>
            <p class="text-parchment text-16 xl:text-19">
              But most importantly, the preschool gives the children a strong foundation of faith through a Christ-centered curriculum.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="project2-section2" class="flex justify-center px-32 md:px-53 lg:px-59 py-59 md:py-95">
    <div class="grow-1 flex flex-col-reverse md:flex-row md:flex-wrap-reverse justify-center items-center gap-95 max-w-559 md:max-w-1281">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-36 w-full md:w-349 md:grow md:shrink-0 md:max-w-644 lg:max-w-none">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
          <H3>The Challenge</H3>
          <p class="text-16">
            Freedom Christian Preschool was just starting up. So they needed a website to promote themselves. 
            Since they were new, they needed a website that stood out, one that rivaled their competitors’ websites.
          </p>
          <p class="text-16">
            Additionally, they were on a tight schedule and needed to start promoting the preschool on billboards and fliers right away. 
            They needed a website <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">as soon as possible</span> so 
            that parents could learn more about the preschool and interested families could get started.
          </p>
          
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
          <H3>The Solution</H3>
          <p class="text-16">
            To solve this, we gave them a two-step solution.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">1.</span>
              <p>
                First, we built them a simple but well-designed, 
                one-page website that gave visitors all the most important information. 
                We completed this preliminary version <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">in just 12 days</span>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-6 ps-6">
              <span class="shrink-0 font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">2.</span>
              <p>
                Then, we started the process of creating a full, 7-page version of the website. 
                We created a custom design for the website, one that was <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">perfect for a preschool</span>. 
                We wanted to make sure that parents would feel comfortable with the preschool on their first website visit. 
                Additionally, we tailored the content to direct visitors to take action and schedule a tour of the preschool.  
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14">
          <H3>The Results</H3>
          <p class="text-16">
            At the end, Freedom Christian Preschool got a website that represents them professionally, 
            one that is <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">better designed than their competitors</span>. 
            They put the web address on their billboards, fliers, and ads. 
            Everything points back to it. It <span class="font-semibold text-cable-shade-2">plays a critical role</span> in getting interested families to enroll.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-59 w-full max-w-300 shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/rski-website-on-mobile.png" 
          alt="Image of the RSKI Riders website on a mobile phone screen" 
          width="300" 
          height="602" 
          loading="lazy"
          class="w-full"
        >

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14 hidden">
          <p class="italic text-16 md:text-21">
            “This is a great spot for a quote or a review if applicable. 
            Larger words. Italics. Says something fantastic about the website or about working with WebCharged.”
          </p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-16 md:text-21">— John Smith</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="flex justify-center bg-blue py-59 px-32 md:px-95">
    <div class="grow-1 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:flex-wrap justify-between justify-center items-center md:items-start gap-59 max-w-559 md:max-w-1281">
      <img 
        class="rounded-md" 
        src="/images/headshot-2-owner-jakin-stahl-480x600.webp" 
        alt="Headshot of the owner Jakin Stahl" 
        width="240" 
        height="300" 
        loading="lazy"
      >
      <div class="md:w-360 grow-1 shrink-0 flex flex-col items-center md:items-start gap-36">
        <H2 color="parchment">Ready to Start Your Own Project?</H2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-14 max-w-700">
          <Text class="text-parchment">
            The first step is to schedule a call with Jakin, the owner. 
            On this call, you can learn more about what we do, and we’ll answer your questions.
          </Text>
          <Text class="text-parchment">
            We want to understand your business better. By doing so, we can help you figure out the solution to your problems. 
          </Text>
        </div>
        <Button class="self-center md:self-start" link="/project-planning-call/" data-umami-event="middle-section-btn-2">Book a call</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>